.\" nmaprs(1) — short man page for the nmaprs / nms binary
.\" Render with:  man -l man/man1/nmaprs.1
.\" Install:      cp man/man1/nmaprs.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH NMAPRS 1 "May 2026" "nmaprs 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nmaprs, nms \- parallel network scanner with nmap-compatible CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nmaprs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGETS ]
.br
.B nms
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGETS ]
.PP
.B nms
is the shorter form of
.BR nmaprs
\(em same binary, quicker to type.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nmaprs
is a Rust-native network scanner that speaks nmap's CLI dialect
.RB ( nmap \-\-help
plus the long-option set from upstream
.BR nmap.cc ).
It implements real TCP connect, UDP, ICMP ping discovery, raw IPv4 /
IPv6 half-open TCP (SYN / NULL / FIN / Xmas / ACK / Window / Maimon),
SCTP (INIT / COOKIE_ECHO), IP-protocol scan
.RB ( \-sO ),
idle scan
.RB ( \-sI ),
FTP bounce
.RB ( \-b ),
target lists / random hosts, IPv6, resume checkpoints, traceroute, and
built-in Rust "scripts" for
.BR \-\-script / \-sC .
.PP
Targets, ports, and timing options accept the same syntax as
.BR nmap (1).
Auto-detects root via
.BR geteuid (2)
and falls back from SYN to TCP connect when unprivileged (use
.B \-\-privileged
to force raw mode).
.PP
.B nmaprs is not a byte-for-byte reimplementation of nmap.
The full NSE Lua runtime is not embedded; OS detection is partial
.RB ( nmap-os-db
MatchPoints scoring for IPv4 only). For authoritative behavior use
.BR nmap (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target Selection
.TP
.B \-\-iL \fIFILE\fR
Input from list of hosts/networks.
.TP
.B \-\-iR \fINUM\fR
Choose
.I NUM
random targets.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude \fITARGETS\fR
Exclude hosts/networks (comma-separated).
.TP
.B \-\-excludefile \fIFILE\fR
Exclude list from
.IR FILE .
.SS Host Discovery
.TP
.B \-sL
List scan \(em simply list targets.
.TP
.B \-sn
Ping scan only (no port scan).
.TP
.BR \-Pn ", " \-\-no-ping
Treat all hosts as online; skip discovery.
.TP
.BI \-PS [ PORTLIST ]
TCP SYN discovery on given ports.
.TP
.BI \-PA [ PORTLIST ]
TCP ACK discovery.
.TP
.BI \-PU [ PORTLIST ]
UDP discovery (default port 40125).
.TP
.BI \-PY [ PORTLIST ]
SCTP INIT discovery (default port 80).
.TP
.B \-PE
ICMP echo.
.TP
.B \-PP
ICMP timestamp request.
.TP
.B \-PM
ICMP address mask request.
.TP
.B \-PR
ARP ping (auto on local IPv4 subnets;
.B \-\-disable-arp-ping
to suppress).
.TP
.B \-n
Never do DNS resolution.
.TP
.B \-R
Always do DNS resolution.
.TP
.B \-\-dns-servers \fISERVERS\fR
Use custom DNS resolvers (comma-separated IPs;
.BR hickory-resolver ).
.TP
.B \-\-system-dns
Use the system resolver.
.TP
.B \-\-traceroute
Trace hop path to each host (concurrent; up to
.B min(parallelism, 32)
subprocesses).
.SS Scan Techniques
.TP
.B \-sS
TCP SYN scan (privileged raw; default when root).
.TP
.B \-sT
TCP connect scan (default when unprivileged).
.TP
.B \-sU
UDP scan.
.TP
.B \-sY
SCTP INIT scan.
.TP
.B \-sZ
SCTP COOKIE_ECHO scan.
.TP
.B \-sA
TCP ACK scan (firewall mapping).
.TP
.B \-sW
TCP Window scan.
.TP
.B \-sN
TCP NULL scan.
.TP
.B \-sF
TCP FIN scan.
.TP
.B \-sX
TCP Xmas scan.
.TP
.B \-sM
TCP Maimon scan.
.TP
.B \-sO
IP protocol scan.
.TP
.BI \-sI " ZOMBIE" [: PROBEPORT ]
Idle scan via a zombie host.
.TP
.BI \-b " FTP"
FTP bounce scan
.RB ( user:pass@host:port ).
.SS Port Specification
.TP
.BI \-p " PORTS"
Port ranges to scan
.RI ( "1-65535" ,
.IR "22,80,443" ,
.B "U:53,T:22"
). Use
.B "\-p \-"
for all 65536.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-ports \fIPORTS\fR
Exclude these ports.
.TP
.B \-F
Fast: scan fewer ports than default (top 100).
.TP
.B \-r
Scan ports sequentially \(em don't randomize.
.TP
.B \-\-top-ports \fIN\fR
Scan the
.I N
highest-ratio ports.
.SS Service / Version / Script
.TP
.BR \-sV ", " \-\-version-scan
Probe open ports to determine service / version info.
.TP
.B \-\-version-intensity \fI0-9\fR
Set version-scan intensity.
.TP
.B \-\-version-light
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-version-intensity\ 2 .
.TP
.B \-\-version-all
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-version-intensity\ 9 .
.TP
.B \-sC
Default scripts (built-in
.B default
+
.B banner
\(em Lua NSE not embedded).
.TP
.B \-\-script \fIEXPR\fR
Run specified built-in scripts.
.SS OS Detection
.TP
.B \-O
Enable OS detection (IPv4: raw probes +
.B nmap-os-db
scoring when
.B \-\-datadir
is set; IPv6: TTL heuristic).
.TP
.B \-\-osscan-limit
OS detect only against promising targets.
.TP
.B \-\-osscan-guess
.RI ( \-\-fuzzy )
Guess OS more aggressively.
.SS Timing & Performance
.TP
.B \-\-timing \fI0-5\fR
Timing template
.RB ( T0
paranoid \(->
.B T5
insane).
.TP
.B \-T \fI0-5\fR
Same as
.BR \-\-timing .
.TP
.B \-\-min-rate \fIN\fR
Send at least
.I N
probes/second.
.TP
.B \-\-max-rate \fIN\fR
Cap probes at
.I N
per second.
.TP
.B \-\-min-parallelism \fIN\fR
.TQ
.B \-M\fR, \-\-max-parallelism \fIN\fR
Concurrent probe count bounds.
.TP
.B \-\-min-hostgroup \fIN\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-hostgroup \fIN\fR
Bound host group sizes; uniform random in
.RB [ min , max ]
when both differ.
.TP
.B \-\-host-timeout \fITIME\fR
Wall-clock per host.
.TP
.B \-\-max-retries \fIN\fR
Extra attempts after probe timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-min-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-initial-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
RTT bounds for adaptive probe timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-scan-delay \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-scan-delay \fITIME\fR
Per-probe delay (uniform random in range when both set).
.TP
.B \-\-stats-every \fITIME\fR
Periodic progress to stderr (% done, ETC, probes/sec).
.SS Firewall / IDS Evasion
.TP
.B \-g \fIPORT\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-source-port \fIPORT\fR
Spoof source port.
.TP
.B \-\-ttl \fIVAL\fR
Set IP TTL.
.TP
.B \-\-badsum
Use bad TCP/UDP/SCTP checksum.
.TP
.B \-D \fIDECOY1,DECOY2,...\fR
Cloak scan with decoys.
.TP
.B \-S \fIIP\fR
Spoof source address.
.TP
.B \-\-data \fIHEX\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-data-string \fITEXT\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-data-length \fIN\fR
Append payload to packets.
.TP
.B \-f
Fragment packets (8-byte default).
.TP
.B \-\-mtu \fIVAL\fR
Custom fragmentation MTU.
.TP
.B \-\-spoof-mac \fIMAC\fR
Spoof source MAC on ARP frames.
.SS Proxy
.TP
.B \-\-proxies \fIURLS\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-proxy \fIURLS\fR
SOCKS4 / HTTP CONNECT proxies for TCP connect scans (comma-separated).
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-oN " " \fIFILE\fR
Normal output.
.TP
.BR \-oG " " \fIFILE\fR
Grepable output.
.TP
.BR \-oX " " \fIFILE\fR
XML output
.RB ( <nmaprun>
root, nmap-compatible).
.TP
.BR \-oA " " \fIBASE\fR
Write all three formats to
.IR BASE .{nmap,gnmap,xml} .
.TP
.BR \-oS " " \fIFILE\fR
Script-kiddie output.
.TP
.BR \-oM " " \fIFILE\fR
Machine-readable (currently same as
.BR \-oG ).
.TP
.B \-\-resolve-all
Scan every resolved address (default: first only).
.SS Misc
.TP
.B \-6
IPv6 targets and scans.
.TP
.B \-A
Aggressive:
.BR \-O " + " \-sV " + " \-sC " + " \-\-traceroute .
.TP
.B \-\-resume \fIFILE\fR
Resume from JSON checkpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-iflist
List network interfaces.
.TP
.B \-\-privileged
Force raw mode.
.TP
.B \-\-unprivileged
Force TCP connect (no raw).
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity. May be repeated
.RB ( \-vv ).
.TP
.B \-d
Increase debug level. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXAMPLES
TCP connect scan of common ports:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs scanme.nmap.org
.fi
.RE
.PP
SYN scan + version detection + OS detection (privileged):
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-sV \-O scanme.nmap.org
.fi
.RE
.PP
Aggressive scan of /24 with grepable output:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-A 192.168.1.0/24 \-oG net.gnmap
.fi
.RE
.PP
UDP scan of top 100 ports through a SOCKS4 proxy:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-sU \-\-top-ports 100 \-\-proxies socks4://127.0.0.1:1080 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Idle scan via a zombie:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sI zombie.example.com:65535 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read targets from file, write all three output formats:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-\-iL targets.txt \-oA scan-results
.fi
.RE
.PP
IPv6 SYN scan with fast (top-100) ports:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-6 \-sS \-F 2001:db8::1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resume an interrupted scan:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-\-resume nmaprs.checkpoint.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
List interfaces:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-\-iflist
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed (regardless of host/port states).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid CLI usage, required privileges missing, or fatal I/O error.
.TP
.B 2
At least one target failed to resolve.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./data/nmap-services
.TQ
.I ./data/nmap-service-probes
.TQ
.I ./data/nmap-os-db
.TQ
.I ./data/nmap-protocols
Nmap reference data (location override via
.BR \-\-datadir
or
.B NMAPDIR
env var).
.TP
.I nmaprs.checkpoint.json
Default checkpoint path for
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/nmaprs.1
.TQ
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/nmaprsall.1
This man page + the full reference.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NMAPDIR
Override the default
.B \-\-datadir
search path for Nmap reference files.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Suppress ANSI color in terminal output.
